							<p class="rt-intro">CLARA compiles to a .NET expression tree that is JIT-compiled to machine code, so a policy is a normal compiled function — not an interpreter walking a tree. This runs the language's conformance suite and then times the reference late-fee policy against the identical rules written by hand in C#, on this machine, right now.</p>
